  23:     - One pixel lies in the upper half and the other in the lower half.
  24:     - The grid height is even so the final border split has a clear midpoint.
  25: 
  26:     Rule:
  27:     - Sort the two pixels from top to bottom.
  28:     - Draw a full horizontal line through each pixel in its own color.
  29:     - Draw the border, then recolor all non-black border and line pixels in the top half to the top color and in the bottom half to the bottom color.
  30: 
  31:     Key insight:
  32:     - The two pixels define both the line rows and the two-color frame: vertical order decides which
  33:       color owns each half of the output.
  34:     """
  35:     # Plan:
  36:     # 1. Parse the input and determine which pixel is top in which is bottom
  37:     # 2. Draw horizontal lines
  38:     # 3. Draw border, colored appropriately
  39: 
  40:     background = Color.BLACK
  41: 
  42:     # 1. Input parsing: find the two single-pixel components and sort by row (top -> bottom).
  43:     pixels = find_components(
  44:         input_grid,
  45:         bg=background,
  46:         connectivity=4,
  47:         monochromatic=True,
  48:         return_format="dict",
  49:     )
  50:     pixels.sort(key=lambda d: int(d["bbox"][0]))  # r0
  51:     assert len(pixels) == 2
  52: 
  53:     # 2. Draw horizontal lines across the row of each pixel, in that pixel's color.
  54:     output_grid = np.full_like(input_grid, background)
  55:     H, W = output_grid.shape
  56:     for p in pixels:
  57:         r0, _c0, _r1, _c1 = p["bbox"]
  58:         color = int(p["color"])
  59:         draw_line(output_grid, r=int(r0), c=0, direction=(0, 1), length=None, color=color)
  60: 
  61:     # 3. Draw border. Then enforce top-half vs bottom-half coloring.
  62:     top_color = int(pixels[0]["color"])
  63:     bottom_color = int(pixels[1]["color"])
  64: 
  65:     # Border (we recolor halves afterwards, so edges get the correct split).
  66:     draw_line(output_grid, r=0, c=0, direction=(0, 1), length=None, color=top_color)        # top edge
  67:     draw_line(output_grid, r=0, c=0, direction=(1, 0), length=None, color=top_color)        # left edge
  68:     draw_line(output_grid, r=H - 1, c=0, direction=(0, 1), length=None, color=bottom_color) # bottom edge
  69:     draw_line(output_grid, r=0, c=W - 1, direction=(1, 0), length=None, color=bottom_color) # right edge
